insecticide and the  card shows you a few things one that has  of course the name of the product the  newer product number or the EPA number  the company and whether it's restricted  use or not in this case there's no  restrictions which means that homeowners  can buy this product and use it if it  was restricted in New York that means  only certified pesticide applicators  could use that product the second  circles  it says Li use yes and that means the  product can be used in Long Island in  some some products leach to to quickly  through the soil and the sandy soils of  Long Island you could have a potential  for groundwater pollution so there are  some chemicals that you cannot use in  Long Island you can use them here in  upstate New York but not in Long Island  so that will tell you that in the square  there's a button called more and you  press that to get the label once you  press that another more detailed card  will come up with more information about  your product it has information about  what type of product in this case it's  an insecticide it's used in home gardens  and ornamental plantings and I want to  point out that it also will have the  signal warning in this case it's warning  it might be caution warning or danger or  I guess poison and the most toxic of  pesticides so that's a good thing to be  able to find if you want to get the  label you press the most recent label  date in this case it's four three nine  2017 so press that the blue highlighted  numbers for the for the most recent  label for this product and what will  come up is a the picture of the label  for safer soap you probably if you had  chosen this product to look at you would  be seeing what's on the left and on the  upper right is the back side of the  label but inside once you purchase a  product to kind of peel away this part  and you see the actual fine print so to  speak of the label how it's used on what  insects the application rates etc in  this case you'll be your eyes would be  better than mine if I could if you could  read that so here's a little tip in  order to read the fine print of a label  you want to swipe your mouse to the  right and sort of magically these three  buttons will appear if you press the  plus button it increases the font size  though you'll be able to read this fine  print and I actually like to use this  because quite frankly a lot of labels  they have to squeeze so much information  into them that the actual physical label  the paper label that's  part of the cat the product is the types  really small so it is really nice to be  able to have this larger be able to  really read it you could print it out  and be able to study the label because  remember the label is the law you have  to apply a chemical according to the  label whether it's organic or not and so  that part of what we want you to learn  is how to quickly access the most  important parts of information for the  label what's the first aid what's the  environmental hazards what's the product  what kind of PPE protective equipment  that you need to wear in order to  protect yourself when using the chemical  those kind of things so we just want you  to be familiar with the aspects of a  label specifically with safety in mind I  hope you have enjoyed this PowerPoint  and good luck searching nice pad  this has been a production of Cornell  University on the web at Cornell edu
 

